Implement user story SKY-002-a: Implement SkyscannerClient class and interfaces

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.ts with the SkyscannerClient class, SearchParams and FlightResult interfaces, global-fetch-based searchFlights method, constructor key validation (including empty-string and precedence rules), HTTP error handling, parse-error handling, and strict opt-in mock mode via MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true'.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/skyscanner/client.ts exports a SkyscannerClient class with constructor({ apiKey?: string }); apiKey is stored as a private field (# prefix or private keyword) and is not publicly readable
- SearchParams interface exported with exactly: origin: string, destination: string, date: string, adults?: number; FlightResult interface exported with exactly: price: number, currency: string, airline: string, departure: string, arrival: string, duration: number, stops: number
- searchFlights uses the Node.js global fetch exclusively — no axios, node-fetch, or other HTTP dependency imported
- Constructor throws a descriptive Error referencing the missing key when: (a) apiKey is omitted and RAPIDAPI_KEY is unset, (b) apiKey is an empty string, (c) RAPIDAPI_KEY is an empty string and no apiKey is provided; when both constructor apiKey and RAPIDAPI_KEY are present, constructor-provided apiKey takes precedence
- searchFlights rejects with an Error including the HTTP status code on 4xx/5xx responses; the Error message does not include the apiKey value anywhere
- searchFlights rejects with a descriptive parse/validation Error when the response body is malformed or missing expected fields
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API equals exactly 'true', searchFlights returns a deterministic non-empty FlightResult[] fixture (≥2 results, valid shape, varying prices for SKY-004 exercisability) without invoking fetch; for any other value (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE'), performs the real fetch call; real HTTP/API failures are never silently replaced with mock data — mock mode activates only via the exact string 'true'
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 with no type errors





